A||||2||montage||Opinion on new wheels||||1||
Z||000000||montage||06-23-2001||08:18 AM||||I'm in the process of purchasing new wheels and tires but I need some opinions on wheels and offsets. I have an 88 formula and want 16X7 (or 16X7.5) on the front and 17X8 on the rear. One set I found are TSW Revo with a 16X7 47mm offset front. The 88 has a 15X6 with a 37mm offset so these Revo wheels according to my calculations would only stick out 2mm would these fit (I will go out and measure when I get a chance)? However, the rears 17X8 35mm offset would stick out 12.7 mm (0.5") since a 15X7 stock has a 35 mm offset. My other choice would be Konig Monsoons 16X7 with a 40mm offset in the front which would stick out 9 mm and the rear would be a 17X8 with a 40 mm offset so they would stick out 7 mm. The last option would be TSW Hockenheim R 16X7.5 40mm offset front (could go to a 40 series 225, the lowest series on a 7" rim in 225 would be a 45 series) and would stick out 19mm with the rear a 17X8 40mm sticking out 7mm. If i did my calculations right I would think the proper offset in the front would be more important the in the rear so I'm leaning toward the TSW Revo 16X7 47mm and 17X8 35mm. Any opinions?? I could really use some help.<P>Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||montage||06-23-2001||12:07 PM||||I just got off the phone with Discount Tire about the TSW Revo 16X7 5-100mm 47mm wheels. They said that the wheel will fit but would rub with the 47mm offset. I just measured the clearance on my stock wheels and I have 3 inches minimum clearance (quick check I'll be more through before I order). So I figure that with a 7" wheel that adds 0.5" on each side of center line and the offset moves the wheel toward the middle almost 0.5" (less 2mm actually 10mm difference) so that adds up to ~1" so wouldn't these wheels acutually be ideal for the 88? I'd still have 2" of clearance but why would Discount Tire say it would rub? Am I missing something, opinions???||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||06-24-2001||09:04 AM||||If you want to keep your scrub radius the same, keep the wheel centerline in the same place.<P>If you want to increase your steering feel slightly, add more width on the inner edge of the wheel than on the outer edge.<P>That would be my concern above and beyond how much they stick out, but you'll probably end up with the same effect either way.<P>Sorry if I'm preaching to the choir.||||reg||1
